jadx, jadx-gui, and apktool are already verified (✅). You can install the remaining five tools—androguard, mobsf, ghidra, bytecode-viewer, and apkanalyzer—on Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) with the commands below.
(Note: Because your browser strips full URLs on copy-paste, every URL below uses concatenated strings "https://..." so nothing gets cut off.)

1. Install androguard & mobsf via pipx

bash
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y pipx openjdk-21-jdk wget unzip curl python3-dev build-essential libmagic1 && \
pipx ensurepath && \
pipx install androguard && \
pipx install mobsf
Use code with caution.

2. Install Ghidra & Bytecode Viewer into /opt

bash
# 1. Install Ghidra (latest release)
rm -rf /tmp/ghidra_dl && mkdir -p /tmp/ghidra_dl && cd /tmp/ghidra_dl && \
GHIDRA_HTML=$(curl -sL "https://github.com""/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/releases/latest") && \
GHIDRA_REL=$(echo "$GHIDRA_HTML" | grep -oE '/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/releases/download/[^"]+PUBLIC_[0-9]+\.zip' | head -n 1) && \
wget -qO ghidra.zip "https://github.com""$GHIDRA_REL" && \
unzip -oq ghidra.zip && \
sudo rm -rf /opt/ghidra && \
sudo mv ghidra_*_PUBLIC /opt/ghidra && \
sudo ln -sf /opt/ghidra/ghidraRun /usr/local/bin/ghidraRun && \
sudo ln -sf /opt/ghidra/ghidraRun /usr/local/bin/ghidra && \
cd ~ && rm -rf /tmp/ghidra_dl

# 2. Install Bytecode Viewer (latest JAR + global launcher)
sudo mkdir -p /opt/bytecode-viewer && \
BCV_HTML=$(curl -sL "https://github.com""/Konloch/bytecode-viewer/releases/latest") && \
BCV_REL=$(echo "$BCV_HTML" | grep -oE '/Konloch/bytecode-viewer/releases/download/[^"]+Bytecode-Viewer-[0-9.]+\.jar' | head -n 1) && \
sudo wget -qO /opt/bytecode-viewer/Bytecode-Viewer.jar "https://github.com""$BCV_REL" && \
sudo tee /usr/local/bin/bytecode-viewer > /dev/null << 'EOF'
#!/usr/bin/env bash
java -jar /opt/bytecode-viewer/Bytecode-Viewer.jar "$@"
EOF
sudo chmod +x /usr/local/bin/bytecode-viewer
Use code with caution.

3. Install apkanalyzer (Android SDK Command-Line Tools)

bash
mkdir -p "$HOME/Android/Sdk/cmdline-tools" && cd /tmp && \
SDK_URL="https://google.com""/android/repository/commandlinetools-linux-11076708_latest.zip" && \
wget -qO cmdline-tools.zip "$SDK_URL" && \
unzip -oq cmdline-tools.zip -d /tmp/sdk_tmp && \
rm -rf "$HOME/Android/Sdk/cmdline-tools/latest" && \
mv /tmp/sdk_tmp/cmdline-tools "$HOME/Android/Sdk/cmdline-tools/latest" && \
rm -rf /tmp/cmdline-tools.zip /tmp/sdk_tmp && \
sudo ln -sf "$HOME/Android/Sdk/cmdline-tools/latest/bin/apkanalyzer" /usr/local/bin/apkanalyzer
Use code with caution.

4. Verify All Nine Mobile Reverse-Engineering Tools

bash
